    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs could personalize practice by adapting explanations based on student errors (e.g., flaging common missteps like sign errors in derivatives). Interactive quizzes with instant feedback, or generating custom problem sets, would make drills engaging. For advanced topics (like proofs), they could act as ‘guided mentors’—prompting deeper questions when students stumble. Just ensure human oversight to avoid over-reliance."
